Apply Z to each clause with target one. Then apply CX from that clause to each nonroot endpoint’s syndrome wire: A=2m-d_0 CX gates, where d_0 is the root degree. C5 uses five Z and eight syndrome CX gates.

Compile the m+\binom m2 singleton/pair candidates once. Each entry stores an n-bit syndrome mask and one or two edge indices. For each candidate, X-conjugate the zero syndrome literals, compute an AND chain through clean scratch, toggle the candidate’s one or two clause targets, and reverse the chain and X conjugations. The comparison does not depend on the target contents. Injectivity permits at most one true predicate, and scratch returns to zero after every predicate.

Every CCX expands into the full fifteen-primitive H/CX/T/T-dagger sequence. For example, the actual beginning of C5 preparation below implements the first controlled counter increment. The full 

