// Complete the controlled increment by toggling the low counter bit.
cx q[0],q[9];

The CCX has H/CX/T/T-dagger counts 2/6/4/3 and preserves the required phases. No relative-phase AND or opaque decoder replaces it. The decoded clause register and all counter/comparison scratch are clean before the assignment Hadamards. The final probabilities are unconditional marginals over all clause/workspace values; cleanup is checked rather than postselected.

